<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Brescia</h1><p class="st-meta">1797 CE – 1797 CE · capital Brescia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A republic proclaimed in Brescia in March 1797 when the city overthrew Venetian rule, one of the blows that hastened the end of Venice.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a> had been a Venetian mainland city since 1426. On 18 March 1797, a few days after <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-bergamo">Bergamo</a>, local patriots backed by French troops and Bergamasque volunteers seized power, expelled the Venetian governor and proclaimed the Brescian Republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The provisional government abolished Venetian institutions, planted liberty trees and raised a national guard. It sent forces to spread the revolt to the Brescian valleys and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-garda">Lake Garda</a> towns, where peasants loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the Church resisted. It depended on French protection, and its leaders sought union with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> republics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> in May 1797, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a> was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a> in late 1797.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1797 CE – 1797 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.46%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl 